Your task is:
Task:
  ID: 42
  Title: Review PR: Add new login flow
  Description: https://github.com/example/repo/pull/99

This is a PR review task: do not write a plan, change code, or call /wrap-up — you are here to review the PR, not to implement anything.

1. Find the PR number or URL from the task description.
2. Check the diff size: `gh pr diff <PR-number> --repo <owner/repo> | wc -l`
3. Choose the review command based on diff size:
   - Small PR (< ~300 lines changed): run `/review`
   - Large PR (≥ ~300 lines changed): run `/review-pr`

After running the review, present your findings and wait for the user's instructions.

Knowledge base: the `/learnings` skill manages it — check it when something is unclear, and record what you find.
